      "urpx:hasCoverageClaim": {
        "@id": "cpau:cc-e-nse-1-2025-09-01",
        "@type": "urpx:CoverageClaim",
        "urpx:completenessResult": {
          "@id": "urpx:partial"
        },
        "urpx:selfContained": true,
        "urpx:explainedBy": {
          "@type": "urpx:Evaluation",
          "@id": "cpau:cc-e-nse-1-2025-09-01-evaluation",
          "urpx:evaluationKind": {
            "@id": "urpx:coverageEvaluation"
          },
          "urpx:description": "This filing does not carry everything its source document states. 1 parts are deferred, listed here in the same words as the filing's tariff.toml [modeling].deferrals so the two records cannot drift. (1) Annual settlement period not modeled. Sheet E-NSE-1 prices the compensation against net surplus electricity accumulated over an annual settlement period: Section A applies the schedule to customers \"who, at the end of an annual settlement period, as described in Rule 29, are Net Surplus Customer-Generators\", and Special Condition 1 states \"Net surplus electricity, as specified in Rule 29, if applicable, will be multiplied by the above compensation rate to determine the Customer's annual net surplus electricity compensation stated in dollars.\" The model carries the $0.1012/kWh rate correctly but has no CalculationMethod and no interval property anywhere, so nothing in it distinguishes this annual true-up credit from a per-interval export credit such as CPAU E-EEC-1; the two models differ only in price value and description prose. Expressible under v0.5.1 and verified by pyshacl against the shapes at abdfb521 (zero new violations): add urpx:intervalDuration \"P1Y\" and urpx:intervalType urpx:annualInterval to cpau:nse-ms-energy-net-surplus, the same MetricSpecification-level pattern pge:ms-energy-annual-rolling already ships. Put it on the MetricSpecification, NOT on the PriceDefinition: clj-urpx 0.31.0 reads urpx:intervalDuration only off a PriceDefinition's CalculationMethod (price.clj recurring-interval), and its presence there excludes the price from the per-kWh marginal, which would be wrong for a genuinely per-unit rate. Leave urpx:intervalAlignment unset: the window's start and end are defined in CPAU Rule 29, which is not held in this corpus, so the alignment cannot be sourced without fetching it. This is work, not a blocker.",
          "urpx:evaluatedOn": "2026-09-22T00:00:00"
        }
      }
    },
    "urpx:modifierUniqueIdentifier": "E-NSE-1"
